From afb64bc7315b45b6600ebc085881150716845ee9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julia Lavrova <jlavrova@google.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 16:19:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [M156] [ganesh] Drop mask domain in SoftwarePathRenderer

Original change's description:
> [ganesh] Drop mask domain in SoftwarePathRenderer
>
> SoftwarePathRenderer::DrawToTargetWithShapeMask passed a CPU-mapped
> maskDomain to GrTextureEffect::MakeSubset. Because GrTextureEffect
> insets nearest-neighbor clamp bounds by 0.5 + 1/512, an exact
> [0.5, size - 0.5] domain for masks larger than 1px never skips the
> shader clamp, whereas float32 rounding under huge cancelled
> translations and non-unit scales can pull maskDomain inward, drop the
> clamp, and sample stale texels from reused approx-fit A8 mask textures.
> Omit maskDomain so approx-fit masks that do not fill the backing
> texture always clamp to maskSubset.
>
> Without the fix, SoftwarePathRenderer_HugeTranslateStaysInMaskSubset
> fails 30 assertions (15 on OpenGL and 15 on Vulkan across scales 1.25
> and 1.5 with translations 1e7 and 3e7, with 62-179 pixels depending on
> stale texels).
>
> Tested:
> - Skia dm --src tests --config gl vk --match SoftwarePathRenderer
>   PathRenderer GrTextureEffect DrawPath ClipStack (44/44 unit tests
>   passed on Linux 7.1.6 x86_64, Debug GN build, GCC 15.2.0, OpenGL and
>   Vulkan)
> - Skia trybot:
>   Test-Ubuntu24.04-Clang-NUC11TZi5-GPU-IntelIrisXe-x86_64-Debug-All-DDL3_ASAN_Vulkan
> - Canary-G3, Canary-Flutter and Canary-Android passed
> - Canary-Chromium: only failure is the known flake
>   conformance/rendering/preservedrawingbuffer-leak.html in
>   webgl2_conformance_webgl_on_webgpu_tests (AMD Linux); the retry
>   without the patch passed 10/10
> Not tested:
> - Metal, Dawn/Graphite, Direct3D, Android/iOS/macOS/Windows GPU drivers
>
